  "entry": "code/README.md",
  "notes": "Found in a public repository and run by a computer-use agent (batch public-1). Given a laminar-flow UV reactor's geometry, flow and fluid properties, it predicts survival (C/C0) with a residence-time-distribution (RTD) model and compares it with a well-mixed model, reports Reynolds and Peclet regime verdicts, and back-solves a microbial rate constant k or an actinometer fluence rate E' from measured C/C0. Data used in the run: example. tree.json is the workflow the agent did and a second agent replayed; run.json says how.",
